pe":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up PR to #115177. I included the changes specific to this PR as a separate commit.\r\n\r\nGiving every pass a unique buffer helps, but we can take this even further by giving every frame its own buffer too. This allows the contents of the buffer to be updated with transfer workers, allowing the copy queue to overlap with the previous frame.\r\n\r\nBefore (1.55 ms, same as the after picture in the other PR):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1771\" height=\"398\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b9ba05d-9906-4a5e-8c27-571e0de0b303\" />\r\n\r\nAfter (1.47 ms):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1749\" height=\"422\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260122_151420\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4946ff2b-d433-4fef-937f-be092e1208f6\" />\r\n\r\nIn the future, we could probably do this for all uniform buffers, maybe through a reusable helper class, to eliminate all copies at the start of the frame.\r\n\r\n## TODO\r\n\r\n- [ ] Check if D3D12 legacy barriers work properly with this.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":nu